  "answer": "In the context of full configuration, 'radio configuration' encompasses not only resource configuration but also other configurations such as MeasConfig, RLC bearer configurations (as configured by RLC-BearerConfig), and in the case of NR-DC or NE-DC, the entire NR or E-UTRA SCG configuration. In an NR-DC scenario, this means that upon full configuration, the UE releases the entire SCG configuration (including its associated radio configurations) as specified in the MR-DC release procedure (5.3.5.10), and then re-establishes it according to the new configuration received in the RRCReconfiguration message. This includes reconfiguring the SCG's RLC bearers, MAC, RLC, and PDCP entities, as well as any associated measurement configurations and logical channel settings.",
