The UE determines it is in MR-DC (Multi-RAT Dual Connectivity) if it is in any of the following states: (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, or NR-DC. Specifically, this occurs when: 
- The UE is in (NG)EN-DC if it is configured with nr-SecondaryCellGroupConfig (as per TS 36.331) and connected to the 5GC (for NGEN-DC) or EPC (for EN-DC); 
- The UE is in NE-DC if it is configured with nr-SecondaryCellGroupConfig and connected to the 5GC; 
- The UE is in NR-DC if it is configured with mrdc-SecondaryCellGroup set to nr-SCG. 
Thus, MR-DC is a collective term encompassing these three configurations.

